---
description: Put each React component in its own file instead of defining it inside another component.
alwaysApply: true
---

# One component per file

When adding a component, create a new file next to the component that uses it and import it. Do not declare a second component in the same file.

```tsx
// questionShareButton.tsx
export default function QuestionShareButton() {}

// questionCard.tsx
import QuestionShareButton from "./questionShareButton";
```

A loading skeleton that only represents that component may stay in the same file. `QuestionCardSkeleton` is its own module in `questionCardSkeleton.tsx`.
